y shift as an  ability itself by linking it to the  condition of the scarlet eyes sort of  like how bisky subconsciously created  her body transformation it was just bred  out of a deeply rooted desire  an effective response to a critical need  which also very much describes garappaka  because you can do  almost literally anything with nen which  is why the idea that karapika is an aura  user has very much actually poisoned any  hope we have  of ever understanding the kurt clan in  their natural form whatever the case  kraka's accomplishments with the eyes  actively break  the established rules of power in hunter  hunter and there is definitely precedent  for that but  most of those instances can be traced  back directly to the dark continent for  example the biological phenomena of the  five threats each one of which would be  capable of wiping out humanity if left  unchecked  these beings all possess seemingly  naturally developed characteristics  unlinked to nenus although the only  argument i could make for one that does  use nen might be i better known as  nanika  and better known than that as alaka and  that's mostly because i have a lot of  trouble believing that the god like wish  granting can exist without  some kind of aura manipulation i mean if  that is the case then  well hunter hunter is certainly broken  but the scarlet eyes are much more akin  to the other dark continent life forms  it seems extremely likely that some sort  of ancient group of what would become  the kurta clan  developed the scala dies as a survival  mechanism to live on the dark continent  and the reason why i pretty immediately  jumped to that conclusion all has to do  with a man by the name of beyond netero  this certified sneaky man said something  quite fascinating in his first  appearance in the series during chapter  340 in a live broadcast announcing not  only the existence of the dark continent  to the world which firstly  wow that was meant to be a bit of a  secret but he a